+## New unreferred result: descent-depth-transition-threshold-alln (23:06:33Z)
+
+The researcher claimed a sharp all-n structural theorem for X_d(n) = permutations of [n] with at
+most d descents, F_d(n) = minimax adaptive-comparison height:
+- (A) n log2(d+1) - log2 C(n+d,d) <= log2|X_d(n)| <= n log2(d+1)
+- (B) n log2(d+1) - log2 C(n+d,d) <= F_d(n) <= n ceil(log2(d+1)) + n
+
+Consequences: F_d(n) = n log2(d+1) + O(n); horn (i) proved (d*=ceil(n/log2 n)=o(n) gives
+F=(1-o(1))log2(n!)); horn (ii) refuted (F_d = Theta(n) iff d=O(1)); a smooth logarithmic ramp,
+not a sharp jump.
+
+### Independent verification (fresh code, not the researcher's)
+
+`/tmp/opencode/exec_ref_descent_verify_20261121.py` (this session) plus my own general
+permutation-family minimax from the prior pass:
+- (A) verified EXHAUSTIVELY for 2<=n<=9, all 1<=d<=n-1, and via an independent Eulerian DP to
+  n=200 (log|X_d|/(n log2(d+1)) -> 1 for d <= n/log n).
+- (B) my from-scratch minimax reproduced F_d for all 2<=n<=6, all d; every value inside the
+  claimed interval. Endpoints: F_{n-1}(6)=S(6)=10, F_1(6)=B(6)=7.
+- I independently re-derived all three proof ingredients: (a) coloring surjection with fibers
+  bounded by nondecreasing sequences C(n+d,d); (b) pi -> sorted-order bijection giving the
+  information bound; (c) adjacent-position scan locating <=d+1 increasing runs + balanced merge
+  giving the upper bound. All sound.
+- Asymptotic consequences checked numerically to n=1e5; convergence to the full constant is slow
+  but correct (log log n / log n correction).
